    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Weather and land",
     "texto": [
      "**The forecast.** It speaks of **borrascas** (low pressure: wind and rain) and **anticiclones** (high pressure: stable weather).\n\n**Rain and storms.** A **chaparrón** is a heavy, short rain. In a storm there are **relámpagos** and **truenos**. Weather verbs have no subject: **llueve**, **nieva**, **graniza**. In the cold, **heladas** fall.\n\n**Temperature.** It can be **templada** (mild), cold or hot. The wind blows.\n\n**Landforms.** A **cordillera** is a chain of mountains; a **llanura**, flat land; a **meseta**, flat high land.\n\n**The coast.** A **cabo** juts into the sea; a gulf and a bay are inlets; an **estrecho** is a passage between two lands.\n\n**Placing.** **Limita al norte con** Francia; **está situado en** el norte; the river **desemboca en** the sea. Population density is inhabitants per square kilometre."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Subjectless verbs and position",
     "texto": [
      "**Weather verbs.** They have no subject: **llueve**, **nieva**, **graniza**, **truena**. With **hay** you name what exists: **hay niebla**, **hay heladas**.\n\n**Placing a location.** **Limita con** + place (**limita al norte con** Francia), **está situado en** + place, **desemboca en** + sea.\n\nCardinal points take **a** (**al norte**, **al oeste**) or **en** (**en el norte**)."
     ],
